[SPEAKER_00]: Fair enough.

20:54.379 --> 21:00.984
[SPEAKER_00]: All right, so... Jeon is as good as his word.

21:02.225 --> 21:15.034
[SPEAKER_00]: He allows you to move into your mother's childhood chambers, which is...

21:17.407 --> 21:18.948
[SPEAKER_00]: A small little room.

21:18.968 --> 21:20.748
[SPEAKER_00]: The size of this room?

21:21.168 --> 21:31.512
[SPEAKER_00]: Probably, but actually it's very similar to the size of this room, about the size of this room, and with a veranda, a deck, that overlooks the cliffs to the royal docks.

21:31.952 --> 21:32.232
[SPEAKER_00]: Nice.

21:32.573 --> 21:34.333
[SPEAKER_00]: Maybe a hundred feet below.

21:34.413 --> 21:36.714
[SPEAKER_00]: No, it's actually very nice.

21:37.134 --> 21:38.615
[SPEAKER_00]: There's an offshoot this way.

21:39.486 --> 21:44.049
[SPEAKER_00]: That is the bedchamber, which is probably about, I would say, 15 feet wide.

21:44.849 --> 21:46.730
[SPEAKER_00]: A very nice bed in there, a table.

21:47.071 --> 21:48.612
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay.

21:48.832 --> 21:50.533
[SPEAKER_00]: And then there's a closet.

21:50.553 --> 21:52.754
[SPEAKER_00]: In fact, I've drawn it for you here.

21:53.735 --> 21:55.456
[SPEAKER_00]: Each one of those things is five feet.

21:56.436 --> 21:57.177
[SPEAKER_00]: So is this the door?

21:58.238 --> 21:59.238
[SPEAKER_00]: This is the door.

21:59.358 --> 22:00.319
[SPEAKER_00]: This is the closet.

22:00.379 --> 22:00.899
[SPEAKER_00]: Closet.

22:01.740 --> 22:02.740
[SPEAKER_00]: This is the veranda.

22:03.061 --> 22:03.621
[SPEAKER_00]: And in fact,

22:06.288 --> 22:09.350
[SPEAKER_00]: This is the balcony outside.

22:09.370 --> 22:11.132
[SPEAKER_00]: There are things that are drawn here.

22:11.152 --> 22:12.473
[SPEAKER_00]: No bathroom?

22:12.773 --> 22:14.174
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, that's down the hall.

22:14.754 --> 22:18.557
[SPEAKER_01]: I don't know if that will work out for me actually.

22:18.797 --> 22:28.284
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, it's a pretty private wing and there are chamber pots and usually you go to the bathroom and the chamber pots

22:29.293 --> 22:32.074
[SPEAKER_00]: And go down to the common bathroom area and pour them out.

22:32.354 --> 22:36.936
[SPEAKER_00]: So that's pretty much how everybody does it in a castle.

22:38.336 --> 22:42.318
[SPEAKER_00]: So by the end of the week, you've moved your stuff into that room.

22:43.798 --> 22:47.079
[SPEAKER_00]: And you've gotten things pretty well set up.

22:48.500 --> 22:49.680
[SPEAKER_00]: The accommodations are good.

22:51.081 --> 22:53.702
[SPEAKER_00]: And you're feeling

23:00.776 --> 23:07.173
[SPEAKER_00]: Disconcerned by the loss of your mother, but you were also feeling like things could have been a lot worse.

23:08.116 --> 23:08.417
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

23:12.121 --> 23:26.873
[SPEAKER_00]: I think that was pretty much the first time you ever talked to your uncle in a way that was sort of genuine and sort of also without your mother's counseling.

23:27.193 --> 23:30.175
[SPEAKER_00]: And you're actually very interested in the way he responded.

23:30.656 --> 23:33.898
[SPEAKER_00]: Because even though it was sort of like, we'll wait and we'll see.

23:34.799 --> 23:35.860
[SPEAKER_00]: It wasn't a no.

23:36.660 --> 23:38.681
[SPEAKER_00]: Which, beforehand, he always gave you.

23:38.921 --> 23:43.563
[SPEAKER_00]: I mean, you have been totally used to hearing no from that guy a lot of times.

23:45.804 --> 23:59.290
[SPEAKER_00]: Anyway, there's news of trouble with the Kingdom of Peoland this week.

24:00.531 --> 24:17.499
[SPEAKER_00]: And apparently there was some kind of conflict happening where the Kiowish fleet is stopping trade merchants from coming to the city of Monmurg.

24:18.159 --> 24:22.821
[SPEAKER_00]: Now, this is very strange because usually

24:25.479 --> 24:35.747
[SPEAKER_00]: The Keoland's Navy would not have a chance or even try such a thing because the Monmurgian Navy would be out there making sure that the trade lanes were open.

24:35.887 --> 24:38.669
[SPEAKER_00]: It's a conflict that Keoland normally cannot deal with.

24:39.509 --> 24:53.199
[SPEAKER_00]: But you feel a strange sense of urgency this month and in a way you kind of become forgotten because there's so many discussions going on with

24:54.352 --> 24:57.793
[SPEAKER_00]: Prince Jeon, other Commodores, and so on.

24:58.153 --> 25:09.217
[SPEAKER_00]: You can't really blame him for, I would say, ignoring you, but... Well, it's already been ignored, but he's made a promise to you that he would look into things for you.

25:09.657 --> 25:16.179
[SPEAKER_00]: However, by the end of the week, after you've moved out, a couple of days have gone by and still he has not summoned you or talked to you.

25:16.639 --> 25:19.940
[SPEAKER_00]: Basically, once again, you've been forgotten in this place.

25:20.521 --> 25:20.841
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay?

25:20.981 --> 25:21.221
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay.

25:22.851 --> 25:32.354
[SPEAKER_00]: You also notice that the guards of the city are on higher alert.

25:33.094 --> 25:46.199
[SPEAKER_00]: And you catch rumors from some of the servants that there actually have been some riots in Lower City and Market Square, which is weird because normally at the beginning of

25:47.903 --> 26:01.331
[SPEAKER_00]: The end of winter, which is kind of where you're at right now, the trade ships start rolling in from around the world to begin trading and selling wares in the great market.

26:02.452 --> 26:04.693
[SPEAKER_00]: So this is weird.

26:05.694 --> 26:06.434
[SPEAKER_00]: There's tension.

26:08.095 --> 26:15.620
[SPEAKER_00]: And for there to be tension in the royal palace, which is usually very much pampered, it's bizarre.

26:17.792 --> 26:32.616
[SPEAKER_00]: Anyway, you get into a routine waiting for your uncle to talk to you.

26:33.637 --> 26:42.159
[SPEAKER_00]: And the days roll by, I'd say a week rolls by before your, I mean since your mother had died.

26:43.139 --> 26:44.400
[SPEAKER_00]: And you find yourself

26:47.286 --> 26:58.263
[SPEAKER_00]: In your room, isolated as usual, sitting there reading a book when you decide to light an opium stick.

26:59.919 --> 27:05.983
[SPEAKER_00]: Go into your bedchamber and go to sleep because, you know, obviously it's been particularly hot.

27:06.683 --> 27:06.904
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

27:06.984 --> 27:07.704
[SPEAKER_00]: Your skin has been itchy.

27:07.724 --> 27:09.966
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, what kind of time of year is it?

27:10.166 --> 27:12.127
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, it's coming into summer.

27:12.367 --> 27:17.931
[SPEAKER_00]: It's like I would say mid-spring, but the

27:21.060 --> 27:29.884
[SPEAKER_00]: The climate in Monmurg is that of, I would say, the Caribbean.

27:30.004 --> 27:33.485
[SPEAKER_01]: I read the thing about what the kind of temperature is here usually.

27:33.885 --> 27:34.866
[SPEAKER_01]: Tropically hot.

27:34.906 --> 27:38.527
[SPEAKER_00]: Think of this as like a Florida or Louisiana type place.

27:39.088 --> 27:42.069
[SPEAKER_00]: That kind of stuff.

27:42.449 --> 27:48.932
[SPEAKER_00]: Normally what you do is you light an opium stick and you close the

27:51.182 --> 28:01.237
[SPEAKER_00]: Curtain's right there, and it fills the room, and it eases the pain and the itching that you have on your body, and you can fall asleep to that fairly easily.

28:01.557 --> 28:04.401
[SPEAKER_00]: So you find yourself doing that.

